-- title:
--   Order at V equals length at the node ring's prime q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ in level $N$ at $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ for $P$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $w$ a place of $k$-the function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, and write $B =$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` for the subring of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` of elements lying in `R.nodeIntegers w` whose Laurent series belongs to `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $j(q)$ and $j(q^{N q})$ in the notation of the project; assume $B$ is noetherian and that every element $z$ of `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K` is a ratio $x/y$ with $x, y \in B$ and $y \neq 0$. Let $V$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `P.reduceFst V = w`, and let $\mathfrak q \subseteq B$ be a prime ideal consisting exactly of those $g \in B$ with $V.\mathrm{evalAt}(g) = 0$ and such that every prime strictly below $\mathfrak q$ is zero. Then for every nonzero $g \in B$, the natural number $(\mathrm{ord}_V g)^+$, viewed in $\mathbb N_\infty$, equals the length of $(B/gB)_{\mathfrak q}$ as a module over $B_{\mathfrak q}$.
--
--   This identifies the order of vanishing of a function at a place of the function field of $X_0(Nq)$ lying over a node with the intersection multiplicity computed as a length at the height-at-most-one prime of the node ring beneath it, the point being that the place is unramified over the localised node ring. It feeds the comparison of degrees with sums of local lengths and the computations of residues of functions at the supersingular nodes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_toNat_ord_eq_length_localizedModule_quotient_of_forall_mem_iff_evalAt_eq_zero.lean

